{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1152485-advice-on-stargazer-concept","id":1152485,"title":"Advice On Stargazer Concept","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-24T06:33:36-07:00","id":1152485,"title":"Advice On Stargazer Concept","content":"My vampire group might be switching games to Werewolf: the Wyld West and we were asked to make characters. Now that the one shot is over, a lot of people were very satisfied with the game and I was thinking making a character with a little more to them so I was planning on a homid Ragabash Stargazer.<br /> <br /> Now the general concept is: You can't solve the problems of the world hidden in a alcove.<br /> <br /> So the idea I had was a Stargazer who is exploring the world on his own time thinking about how to solve problems. Kind of Kung Fu-ish (which that thought only occurred after I had the character sheet filled). Unlike some of the rest of his tribe, he believes you must see the problems that afflict men and garou alike in order to solve them. So I spent a lot of different lores, enigmas, and crafts. His primary is also mental. He enthusiastically wonders the world until he arrives in New York. I thought it would be interesting to have him overly curious.<br /> <br /> Any initial thoughts?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19321-kewlimp","name":"kewlimp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T07:50:29-07:00","id":1152505,"title":"","content":"The main character in the story portion of W20 Rage Across the World sounds a lot like the character you are purposing. You may want to review that source for more ideas. If nothing else it gives come examples of Gifts that your character may have picked up on his travels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T08:44:54-07:00","id":1152519,"title":"","content":"This would be the third time this has happened. I've accidentally created a character that already exists that in a story I've not yet read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19321-kewlimp","name":"kewlimp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-24T10:28:01-07:00","id":1152550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kewlimp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1152485-advice-on-stargazer-concept?p=1152519#post1152519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would be the third time this has happened. I've accidentally created a character that already exists that in a story I've not yet read.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The character in the story is a CoG and he is just traveling to travel. So there are differences, but the things he goes through on his travels would make for an interesting story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T07:29:37-07:00","id":1153731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kewlimp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1152485-advice-on-stargazer-concept#post1152485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now the general concept is: You can't solve the problems of the world hidden in a alcove.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's why you don't play Stargazers =P<br /> They have this strong NPC vibe and are really perfect for the hermit that stays in a corner of the world and occasionally meets with the PC, but it's really hard to put them into a more active role without making it look stretched, especially if we're talking of a prolonged task.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T12:06:29-07:00","id":1153773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1152485-advice-on-stargazer-concept?p=1153731#post1153731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's why you don't play Stargazers =P<br /> They have this strong NPC vibe and are really perfect for the hermit that stays in a corner of the world and occasionally meets with the PC, but it's really hard to put them into a more active role without making it look stretched, especially if we're talking of a prolonged task.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that's why there were no starting sample characters in either Stargazers tribebook.<br /> <br /> Wait, no, there they are. Guess that's not true. And there's even mentioning of &quot;Stargazers are not a splat of cloistered D&amp;D monks&quot; in the Revised tribebook, because apparently that's a thing that needs to be spelled out after so much fanon cruft scumming up the setting for so long. Whatever the formula was, it could probably do with another infusion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T12:19:44-07:00","id":1153778,"title":"","content":"A decently nuanced take on Kwai-chang kane is pretty much the gold standard for a Stargazer. You might want to add in some ways he teaches lessons as a Trickster, but honestly your concept sounds pretty solid","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-28T13:07:42-07:00","id":1153786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1152485-advice-on-stargazer-concept?p=1153773#post1153773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, that's why there were no starting sample characters in either Stargazers tribebook.<br /> <br /> Wait, no, there they are. Guess that's not true. And there's even mentioning of &quot;Stargazers are not a splat of cloistered D&amp;D monks&quot; in the Revised tribebook, because apparently that's a thing that needs to be spelled out after so much fanon cruft scumming up the setting for so long. Whatever the formula was, it could probably do with another infusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Slow down mate, Asshole Road won't take you in pleasant places. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-30T13:47:26-07:00","id":1154210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1152485-advice-on-stargazer-concept?p=1153773#post1153773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, that's why there were no starting sample characters in either Stargazers tribebook.<br /> <br /> Wait, no, there they are. Guess that's not true. And there's even mentioning of &quot;Stargazers are not a splat of cloistered D&amp;D monks&quot; in the Revised tribebook, because apparently that's a thing that needs to be spelled out after so much fanon cruft scumming up the setting for so long. Whatever the formula was, it could probably do with another infusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The pop idol character template from the revised book is still one of my all time favorites.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, one of the common things in Zen Buddhist traditions is that after one reaches that initial state of insight into one's nature, part of the next step in the process is to express the philosophy in daily life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">One can easily get the impression that realization, kensh\u014d, an experience of enlightenment, or however you wish to phrase it, is the end of Zen training. It is not. It is, rather, a new beginning, an entrance into a more mature phase of Buddhist training. To take it as an ending, and to &quot;dine out&quot; on such an experience without doing the training that will deepen and extend it, is one of the greatest tragedies of which I know. There must be continuous development, otherwise you will be as a wooden statue sitting upon a plinth to be dusted, and the life of Buddha will not increase.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div>- <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Rev. Master Jiyu-Kennett</span></span></span><br /> <br /> In the case of the Stargazers, this usually means going out into the world and confronting the illusions and evils which plague it. Or go out and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shaolin_Soccer\" target=\"_blank\">form a soccer team</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 10-30-2017, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T07:17:57-07:00","id":1154366,"title":"","content":"I would have rolled a Nuwisha, but for some reason the ST hates coyotes in real life and doesn't want one in the game. I'm not super surprised by it. One of my philosophies about role playing is playing new things. Never played a character like this and thought it would be a change of pace. Thanks for the feedback.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19321-kewlimp","name":"kewlimp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T09:21:53-07:00","id":1154407,"title":"","content":"You're better off with the Stargazer concept over the Nuwisha anyway, especially if your group is going into WTA (WW) new to the game, everyone being Werewolves is a lot simpler than people trying to play other shifters and then get along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T11:32:21-07:00","id":1154450,"title":"","content":"It was fun. Only time I've ever seen a Get Ahroun run from a fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19321-kewlimp","name":"kewlimp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T12:43:07-07:00","id":1154473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1152485-advice-on-stargazer-concept?p=1154407#post1154407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're better off with the Stargazer concept over the Nuwisha anyway, especially if your group is going into WTA (WW) new to the game, everyone being Werewolves is a lot simpler than people trying to play other shifters and then get along.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nuwisha are a bit of a special case, since one of their typical pastimes is passing themselves off as Garou. Kitsune away from Beast Courts territory could probably manage the same ruse for a while. It's one of the advantages of being a different kind of canid shifter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T13:02:13-07:00","id":1154484,"title":"","content":"With a fairly small group - say three players, maybe four at the very most - I think you could do a Fera trickster chronicle with a Nuwisha, Kitsune, Corax and (maybe) Ceilican fairly easily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T13:18:26-07:00","id":1154489,"title":"","content":"I fear for local populaces everywhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19321-kewlimp","name":"kewlimp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T20:14:11-07:00","id":1154954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1152485-advice-on-stargazer-concept?p=1154473#post1154473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Nuwisha are a bit of a special case, since one of their typical pastimes is passing themselves off as Garou. Kitsune away from Beast Courts territory could probably manage the same ruse for a while. It's one of the advantages of being a different kind of canid shifter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ...only if you're around the dumbest Garou ever. A fox is pretty damned different from Wolves on all fronts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T20:46:26-07:00","id":1154971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1152485-advice-on-stargazer-concept?p=1154954#post1154954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> ...only if you're around the dumbest Garou ever. A fox is pretty damned different from Wolves on all fronts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that any fox engaging in this activity is likely to have some serious disguise capabilities, it's probably a bit more difficult to see past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}